#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
fatpix_matrix.py
A one-file Unicode fat-pixel terminal color wall and tiny LED marquee.

Run:
  python3 fatpix_matrix.py
  echo "hello world" | python3 fatpix_matrix.py
  python3 fatpix_matrix.py --no-marquee
  python3 fatpix_matrix.py --file firmware.bin
  cat notes.txt | python3 fatpix_matrix.py --file -

File view:
  arrows / wasd   move byte cursor
  PgUp / PgDn     move cursor by half the visible page
  - / =           small zoom step out / in
  _ / +           larger zoom jump out / in
  1-6             analysis lenses
  i               inspector overlay
  , / .           inspector previous / next page (HEX wraps to DIFF HEX)
  mouse click      select one exact fat-pixel byte range
  mouse drag       extend selection as one contiguous byte range
  :dump FILE       write the selected bytes to FILE
  C               ask optional Clarity for a structural overlay
  ?               help from every interactive state

Paint / board:
  arrows / hjkl   move paint cursor
  space / enter   paint selected color
  1-9             select color
  x               erase to black
  c               clear to black
  f               fill with selected color
  n               noise burst

Animation modes:
  w               wave / interference field
  d               drip / falling smear
  r               rain / falling trails
  s               spark / diffuse decay
  m               marquee / piped or :text message
  i               idle / manual paint

Animation and display:
  a               pause / resume
  [ / ]           slower / faster
  g               glyph / ANSI skin
  R               rotate display palette (Unicode skin only)
  ?               help overlay (pauses animation)
  :               command line
  q / Ctrl-C      quit

Commands:
  clear [color]
  fill <color>
  noise [0.0-1.0] [colors...]
  mode idle|wave|drip|rain|spark|marquee
  speed <fps>
  text <message>
  save <file>
  load <file>

Colors are 0-8 or names: black white red blue orange yellow green purple brown.
Saved files are plain Unicode-square boards.

When stdin is piped, fatpix reads the message to EOF and uses /dev/tty for keys.
Use --no-marquee to ignore piped stdin and launch the normal wall instead.
"""

